# The build context is what the Dockerfile COPYs: go.mod, go.sum, cmd/, internal/
# and web/. Everything else stays out of it, and so do local build products: the
# image always builds the frontend itself, from a clean `npm ci`.

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local configuration and state (secrets, the SQLite database).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal

# Local build output. A host-built node_modules may be for another OS or libc
# (musl in the image), and a stale dist would be embedded in place of a fresh one.
**/node_modules
web/dist
internal/webui/dist/*
!internal/webui/dist/.gitkeep
bin
berth

# Not part of the backend image.
images
traefik
docker-compose.yml
README.md
CLAUDE.md
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
